{
  "_doc": "Evidence behind the docs/RESULTS.md 2026-08-19 book-boundary-crop rows. 'before' = book_crop.enabled false (the shipped v0.2.0 behaviour), 'after' = v0.3.0 defaults. Both arms call the SAME code paths, so the comparison is like-for-like. The gutter table is the load-bearing metric (testset/gt/gutter.json); clipped_pct_of_labelled_book grades the emitted crop against the six hand labels in testset/gt/book_box.json and must be 0.0. The OCR table is from the real seven-stage run (pipeline.run_all) on the four zoomset sets, NOT an ad-hoc harness; treat its word counts as indicative only \u2014 whole-image OCR at psm 3 was measured to churn +/-60 words in BOTH directions under reframing, so it supports the STRUCTURAL claim (a subpage that was background is now a page) and not a fine-grained accuracy claim.",
